.TH HOTSPOT\-HUB\-CLI 1 "October 2026" "Hotspot Hub 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
hotspot\-hub\-cli \- command-line interface for Hotspot Hub
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hotspot\-hub\-cli
[\fB\-h\fR]
.IR command
[\fIargs\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hotspot\-hub\-cli
is the command-line companion to Hotspot Hub, a lightweight concurrent Wi-Fi Access Point (AP) controller for Linux systems.
It allows inspecting status, starting or stopping the hotspot, listing and disconnecting connected stations, managing 2.4GHz/5GHz frequency bands, configuring WPA2/WPA3 security, and administering MAC address access control lists.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Display comprehensive status information including hotspot activation state, active security protocol (WPA2 or WPA3-SAE), uplink station details, client counts, DHCP lease status, MAC filter enforcement state, WARP status, and VPN bypass routing priority.
.TP
.B on
Ensure virtual interface \fBap0\fR exists and activate the NetworkManager hotspot connection profile.
.TP
.B off
Deactivate the hotspot connection profile.
.TP
.B restart
Cycle the hotspot connection off and back on.
.TP
.B clients
List currently associated Wi-Fi stations on the AP interface, including MAC addresses, signal strength (dBm), and active DHCP leases.
.TP
.BI kick " <mac>"
Disconnect an active client station identified by its MAC address using \fBiw dev ap0 station del\fR.
.TP
.B qr
Display hotspot SSID, passphrase, and render a terminal-friendly UTF-8 QR code for mobile device scanning (requires \fBqrencode\fR).
.TP
.BI band " [2.4GHz|5GHz|Auto]"
View current Wi-Fi band configuration and available hardware channels, or modify the active band. Available hardware channels on the Wi-Fi PHY are validated prior to profile application.
.TP
.BI mac\-filter " <action> [mac]"
Manage MAC filtering access policies and list entries:
.RS
.TP
.B list
Display filter operational state (enabled/disabled, mode) and show all allowed and blocked MAC addresses.
.TP
.B enable
Enable active MAC address filtering.
.TP
.B disable
Disable active MAC address filtering.
.TP
.BI allow " <mac>"
Add a normalized MAC address to the allowed list (\fBallowed_macs.txt\fR).
.TP
.BI deny " <mac>"
Add a normalized MAC address to the blocked list (\fBblocked_macs.txt\fR).
.TP
.BI remove " <mac>"
Remove a MAC address from both allowed and blocked lists.
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show summary of command-line options and subcommands.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HOTSPOT_HUB_STA_IF
Station (uplink) wireless network interface name. Default is \fBwlan0\fR.
.TP
.B HOTSPOT_HUB_AP_IF
Access Point virtual network interface name. Default is \fBap0\fR.
.TP
.B HOTSPOT_HUB_CON
NetworkManager connection profile name for the hotspot. Default is \fBHotspot\-Shared\fR.
.TP
.B HOTSPOT_HUB_DOCS
Path to project documentation.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/hotspot\-hub/config.json
JSON configuration storing MAC filter state, frequency band preference, and detected WPA3-SAE hardware support.
.TP
.I ~/.config/hotspot\-hub/allowed_macs.txt
Plain-text list of permitted client MAC addresses (one per line).
.TP
.I ~/.config/hotspot\-hub/blocked_macs.txt
Plain-text list of denied client MAC addresses (one per line).
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/hotspot\-hub/hotspot\-hub.log
Persistent rotating log file.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Show overall system and hotspot status:
.RS
.B hotspot\-hub\-cli status
.RE
.PP
Switch AP operation to 5GHz band:
.RS
.B hotspot\-hub\-cli band 5GHz
.RE
.PP
Add a trusted smartphone MAC to the allowlist:
.RS
.B hotspot\-hub\-cli mac\-filter allow 00:11:22:33:44:55
.RE
.PP
Disconnect an unauthorized station immediately:
.RS
.B hotspot\-hub\-cli kick 00:11:22:33:44:55
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hotspot\-hub (1),
.BR nmcli (1),
.BR iw (8),
.BR qrencode (1)
